From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 12:54:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] check_boot_jars: allow oplus-fwk OEM stub packages on the
 bootclasspath (minimal)

The full crDroid boot-jars-package-check rejects hardware/oplus/oplus-fwk/
oplus-fwk.jar because com.oplusx.sysapi.cryptoeng is not in
package_allowed_list.txt. This namespace is load-bearing for the AIUnit
CryptoengNative SDK, the oplus-fwk CryptoEng HAL client, and FIDO attestation.

Add the mandatory com.oplusx.* namespace. Keep the coloros.deepthinker and
itgsa.opensdk.wm namespaces documented but inactive until APK-linkage proof
shows a live shipped consumer.
---
 scripts/check_boot_jars/package_allowed_list.txt | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scripts/check_boot_jars/package_allowed_list.txt b/scripts/check_boot_jars/package_allowed_list.txt
--- a/scripts/check_boot_jars/package_allowed_list.txt
+++ b/scripts/check_boot_jars/package_allowed_list.txt
@@ -300,6 +300,14 @@ vendor\.oplus\..*
 com\.oneplus\..*
 vendor\.oneplus\..*
 
+# infiniti camera-port v3: oplus-fwk boot-jar OEM stub namespaces missing from crDroid base.
+# MANDATORY: com.oplusx.sysapi.cryptoeng is load-bearing for AIUnit CryptoengNative,
+# the cryptoeng HAL client, and FIDO attestation.
+com\.oplusx\..*
+# CONDITIONAL: activate only after APK-linkage proof shows a live shipped consumer.
+# com\.coloros\.deepthinker
+# com\.itgsa\.opensdk\.wm
+
 # QC adds
 com.qualcomm.qti
 com.quicinc.tcmiface
-- 
